 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 177,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Prostate cancer: SCREEN or not? Once found, WATCH, CURE or CONTROL?",
   "lines": [
    "EARLY disease is SILENT: found by prostate-specific antigen (PSA) or a nodule on rectal exam",
    "LATE: bone pain, anemia, weight loss, fatigue = metastases · risk: age, family history, African ancestry"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_s",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 240,
   "h": 116,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "NO symptoms: a SHARED decision",
   "lines": [
    "catches curable cancer, but also harmless ones: false positives, biopsy harm"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_d",
   "x": 325,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 744,
   "h": 116,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "PSA ↑ or a NODULE → TRANSRECTAL ULTRASOUND BIOPSY (imaging alone CANNOT diagnose it)",
   "lines": [
    "GRADE (Gleason): ≤ 6 well differentiated · 7 moderate · 8–10 anaplastic",
    "STAGE: rectal exam · PSA > 50 = spread beyond the gland · bone scan + computed tomography (CT) only if HIGH risk"
   ]
  },
